{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>My eyes</b> — The correct interpretation in my eyes: the meaning of \"net\" is the desire of the evil inclination, and the soul is caught in the net of desire. This is by way of analogy. And if HaShem does not help him, he has no power to escape from the wicked one. Therefore, \"He will bring him out.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:32.987023051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}